      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Write ${8}^{1/7}$ using radical notation.",
      "worked_solution": "The fractional exponent ${x}^{1/n}$ can be written as the radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}.$\n\nComparing ${x}^{1/n}$ with ${8}^{1/7},$ we get $x=8$ and $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{8}^{1/7}=\\sqrt[7]{8}.\n$$",
