    "q-69218": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69218",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{5}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as ${x}^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[3]{5},$ we get $x=5,$ and $n=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{5}={5}^{1/3}\n$$",
