    "q-69229": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69229",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${6}^{3/7}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the power law for exponents, we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n{6}^{3/7}={({6}^{3})}^{1/7}.\n$$\n\nThe fractional exponent ${x}^{1/n}$ can be written as the radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}.$\n\nComparing ${x}^{1/n}$ with our expression above, we get $x={6}^{3}$ and $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{({6}^{3})}^{1/7}=\\sqrt[7]{{6}^{3}}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
