    "q-99490": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99490",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "${5}^{3/4}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, using the power law for exponents, we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n{5}^{3/4}={({5}^{3})}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nThe fractional exponent ${x}^{1/n}$ can be written as the radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}.$\n\nComparing ${x}^{1/n}$ with our expression above, we get $x={5}^{3}$ and $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{({5}^{3})}^{1/4}=\\sqrt[4]{{5}^{3}}.\n$$",
